            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [...] as soon as the loop has a lastprivate variable. In practice that's every such loop, since the target always gets one\n\nMy current thought is to do better about identifying variables that are never used after the loop (which has to be a decent number of loop targets). That would let a good chunk of code work in clang (and the remainder could get an informative `#error`). I'll do this in the near future unless you tell me you have a better plan.",
